    "body": "<p>Learn about the path from a placed order to a submitted review, including how Klaviyo makes it easy to see every order’s status in your review pipeline. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JP0HY3JA3B25M7DNE3CYABXK\">About the Orders tab</h2>\n<p>If you navigate to <strong>Reviews &gt; Orders</strong>, you’ll see a list of recent orders and their review pipeline status. Use this page to understand when someone will receive a review request, make changes to review request timing, and more. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JP0HY3JA2TCHZ4CWRR4B4D46\">Request statuses</h2>\n<p>In the <em>Request status</em> column of the <strong>Orders</strong> tab, every order’s review pipeline status is listed. The following statuses are available: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong><strong>Queued</strong></strong><br>\n<strong>The </strong><strong><em>Ready to review</em></strong><strong> event has been scheduled for a future date/time, based on your settings. </strong>\n</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Ready to review</strong><br>\nA <em>Ready to review</em> event has been triggered for this order. Head to the customer’s profile to confirm they’ve received the first message of your review request flow. Note that a review request may not have been sent if the profile failed your flow’s filters, or if you have a time delay in the flow. </li>\n<li>\n<strong>Reviewed</strong><br>\nThe customer has reviewed one or more items from the order. </li>\n<li>\n<strong>Excluded</strong><br>\nThe order was not eligible for review because all items in it were <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/16684841274139\">excluded</a>.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Usage limit</strong><br>\nYou have a review plan that is too small for your order volume. Upgrade your reviews plan for higher volume. It is not currently possible to re-trigger a review request for an order skipped due to usage limits. </li>\n<li>\n<strong>Missing data</strong><br>\nThe order is missing necessary data. Most often, this means the product IDs in the order don’t match any product IDs in your Klaviyo catalog.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JP0HY3JAY4Q5XY59HYSDEXPV\">How to manually adjust review timing</h2>\n<p>If a review is currently <em>Queued</em>, you can elect to trigger the review request immediately. Note that this will only initiate the review request flow; if the recipient fails the flow’s filters, isn’t eligible to receive marketing messages, or if the flow is not live, then they will not receive a review request. </p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>This process is not immediate. Once you click <strong>Skip waiting time</strong>, it may take several minutes for the <em>Ready to review</em> event to fire. </p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"h_01JP0HY3JAYBZT94Y0PK1V19N9\">Skip waiting time for a single order</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Reviews &gt; Orders</strong>. </li>\n<li>Locate an order with the review status <em>Queued</em>. </li>\n<li>Click the three dots icon to open an additional options menu. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Skip waiting time</strong>. </li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"h_01JP0HY3JAYVW0KS9KN8TYRJV7\">Skip waiting time for all queued orders</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Reviews &gt; Orders</strong>. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Actions</strong>. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Skip waiting time</strong>.</li>\n</ol>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
